---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ipsas/ipsas37.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  covers={metadata.covers}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Objective, Scope & Definitions" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Joint Control — the Unanimous Consent Test" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Types of Joint Arrangement — Operation vs Venture" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Joint Operations — the Look-Through Recognition Model" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Non-Controlling Parties & Acquisitions of Interests in Joint Operations" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Joint Ventures — the Equity Method" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Separate Financial Statements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Transitional Provisions — Joint Ventures: Proportionate Consolidation to the Equity Method" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Transitional Provisions — Joint Operations: Equity Method to Assets & Liabilities" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Effective Date & Amendment Timeline" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IFRS 11" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement / Process Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards — Cross-Reference Map" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Quick-Reference Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <LifecycleNotice
    type="active"
    explanation="IPSAS 37 Joint Arrangements is the current, active standard issued by the IPSASB for accounting by entities that are parties to joint arrangements — distinguishing joint operations (look-through) from joint ventures (equity method). Effective for periods beginning on or after 1 January 2017 (earlier application encouraged). Paras. 1–38. It supersedes IPSAS 8."
    historical="IPSAS 37 is the IPSASB's adaptation of IFRS 11 Joint Arrangements for the public sector — retaining the joint-operation vs joint-venture distinction and the unanimous-consent control test, with public-sector commentary on service delivery partnerships."
    link=""
    linkText=""
  />

  <!-- ============ SECTION 1 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Objective, Scope &amp; Definitions (paras. 1–7)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci">
      <div class="ctitle ci">Objective &amp; scope (para. 1)</div>
      <div class="principle">Establishes principles for financial reporting by entities with an interest in JOINTLY controlled arrangements — requiring them to determine the TYPE of arrangement (operation or venture) and account for it accordingly.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="card cd">
      <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions</div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Joint arrangement</div><div class="glossary-def">A contract or arrangement that gives two or more parties joint control.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Joint control</div><div class="glossary-def">Joint decision-making authority over the relevant decisions of the arrangement.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 2 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Joint Control — the Unanimous Consent Test (paras. 9–18)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">Joint control (para. 9)</div>
      <div class="principle">Joint control exists when decisions about the relevant decisions of the arrangement require the UNANIMOUS consent of the partners — i.e. a simple majority is NOT enough. This is the gateway test for all joint-arrangement accounting.</div>
      <div class="callout warn">In the public sector, joint control frequently arises over shared infrastructure, regional services and cross-boundary projects.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 3 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Types of Joint Arrangement — Operation vs Venture (paras. 19–22)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw">
      <div class="ctitle cw">The split (para. 19)</div>
      <div class="principle">A joint arrangement is a JOINT OPERATION if it is jointly controlled AND the partners have JOINT RIGHTS to the assets, liabilities, revenue and expenses — accounted for on a LOOK-THROUGH basis. It is a JOINT VENTURE if it is jointly controlled but does NOT give joint rights to the assets/liabilities — accounted for using the EQUITY METHOD.</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Type</span><span>Accounting</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Joint operation</span><span>Look-through (share of A/L, revenue, expense)</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Joint venture</span><span>Equity method (IPSAS 36)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 4 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Joint Operations — the Look-Through Recognition Model (paras. 23–24)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">Your share (para. 23)</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Item</span><span>Recognise</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Jointly controlled assets</span><span>Right to use (asset)</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Jointly controlled liabilities</span><span>Your share of obligation</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Revenue from joint activity</span><span>Your share of revenue</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Expenses incurred</span><span>Your share of expense</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout info callout--flush">No goodwill arises in a joint operation — the partners hold the underlying assets directly.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 5 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Non-Controlling Parties &amp; Acquisitions of Interests in Joint Operations (paras. 24A–26)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">Third parties (para. 24A)</div>
      <div class="principle">Where a joint operation includes NON-CONTROLLING parties (the partners do not jointly own 100%), those parties' share of the joint operation's assets/liabilities/revenue/expenses is recognised in the same way — on a look-through basis — and disclosed.</div>
      <div class="callout warn">Acquisition of an additional interest in a joint operation: treat the difference between cost and the previous carrying amount of the acquired share as an adjustment to the joint operation account (equity-method-like for JVs).</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 6 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Joint Ventures — the Equity Method (paras. 27–28)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card cw">
      <div class="ctitle cw">Equity method (para. 27)</div>
      <div class="principle">A joint venture (jointly controlled but no joint rights to assets/liabilities) is accounted for using the EQUITY METHOD per IPSAS 36 — recognise the investor's share of the JV's profit/loss and OCI, and adjust for dividends received. See IPSAS 36 for full mechanics.</div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Look-through</div><div class="glossary-def">Recognition of the investor's share of underlying assets and liabilities.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 7 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Separate Financial Statements (paras. 29–30)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">Separate option (para. 29)</div>
      <div class="principle">In separate financial statements, a joint arrangement may be accounted for under the cost model (IPSAS 31 intangibles / IPSAS 17) instead of look-through — but the equity method remains available for joint ventures.</div>
      <div class="callout info callout--flush">Transition uses the same IPSAS 33 first-time-adoption approach if moving from a prior framework.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 8 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Transitional Provisions — Joint Ventures: Proportionate Consolidation to the Equity Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">Old to new (para. 31)</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Before IPSAS 37</span><span>After IPSAS 37</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.3fr;"><span>Proportionate consolidation</span><span>Equity method (IPSAS 36)</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout warn">Apply retrospectively; restate prior periods as if the equity method had always been used.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 9 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Transitional Provisions — Joint Operations: Equity Method to Assets &amp; Liabilities</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card cw span2">
      <div class="ctitle cw">Remodel (para. 37)</div>
      <div class="principle">Where an existing joint operation was previously accounted for under the equity method (pre-IPSAS 37), the entity retrospectively recognises its share of the underlying assets and liabilities of the arrangement, with a corresponding adjustment to retained earnings at the date of transition.</div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Retrospective application</div><div class="glossary-def">Apply as if the new model had always been used; adjust retained earnings.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 10 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Effective Date &amp; Amendment Timeline (paras. 42–42E)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">Timeline</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;"><span>Date</span><span>Event</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;"><span>Jan 2015</span><span>Issued</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;"><span>1 Jan 2017</span><span>Effective date</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;"><span>2023</span><span>Amended (latest)</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout info callout--flush">IPSAS 37 superseded IPSAS 8 (Interests in Joint Ventures); transition is prospective with retrospective restatement.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 11 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 11</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card cd">
      <div class="ctitle cd">Twin (para. 42F)</div>
      <div class="principle">IPSAS 37 mirrors IFRS 11 — the joint-operation look-through model and joint-venture equity method, the unanimous-consent control test, and the proportionate-consolidation-to-equity-method transition — with public-sector commentary on shared service delivery.</div>
      <div class="cross-list"><span>IFRF 11 joint control</span><span>IPSAS 37 same</span><span>IFRS 11 operation vs venture</span><span>IPSAS 37 same</span><span>IFRS 11 transition</span><span>IPSAS 37 same</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 12 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement / Process Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid grid-spaced">
    <div class="card ci span2">
      <div class="ctitle ci">Where it flows</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1.3fr;"><span>Process</span><span>Ledger</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1.3fr;"><span>Partner allocation</span><span>Joint-Activity Register → share split</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1.3fr;"><span>JV equity accounting</span><span>Associate Module → equity method</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1.3fr;"><span>Transition</span><span>JV Transition Module → retrospective</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 13 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards — Cross-Reference Map</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2">
      <div class="ctitle cd">See also</div>
      <div class="td-table">
        <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Relation</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>IPSAS 36</span><span>Equity-method joint ventures</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>IPSAS 35</span><span>Consolidation (control vs joint control)</span></div>
        <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>IPSAS 33</span><span>First-time transition</span></div>
        <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>IFRS 11</span><span>Direct equivalent</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ SECTION 14 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Joint control</div><div class="glossary-def">Decisions require unanimous consent of partners.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Joint operation</div><div class="glossary-def">Jointly controlled with joint rights; look-through.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Joint venture</div><div class="glossary-def">Jointly controlled, no joint rights; equity method.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Look-through</div><div class="glossary-def">Recognise share of underlying assets/liabilities.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Proportionate consolidation</div><div class="glossary-def">Pre-37 method; now equity method.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Service delivery partnership</div><div class="glossary-def">Typical public-sector joint arrangement over infrastructure.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>

